From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: make the user documentation optional

gnome.yelp() runs itstool to merge translations into the help pages, and
subdir('help') is unconditional, so configure stops on a build that has no
itstool:

  help/meson.build:31:6: ERROR: Program 'itstool' not found or not executable

Add a help option, defaulting to true so nothing changes for anyone building
normally, and skip the subdir when it is off.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -24,3 +24,8 @@
 option('soup2', type : 'boolean', value : false, description : 'build with libsoup2')
 option('opensuse-distro-upgrade', type : 'boolean', value : false, description : 'enable opensuse-distro-upgrade support')
 option('dkms', type : 'boolean', value : false, description : 'enable DKMS plugin to help installing DKMS (and akmods) Secure Boot certificates to UEFI MOK')
+option('help',
+  type: 'boolean',
+  value: true,
+  description: 'Build the user documentation with yelp (needs itstool)'
+)
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -314,7 +314,9 @@
 endif
 subdir('po')
 subdir('doc')
-subdir('help')
+if get_option('help')
+  subdir('help')
+endif
 
 # FIXME: remove when https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson/issues/837 fixed
 meson.add_install_script('meson_post_install.sh')
